(r"Three strengths. Weak: even the whole spread is below the order cost, so no one trades and entry is at its floor. Strong: even the lowest gain exceeds the order cost, so both correct orders occur, and only a purchase lifts the belief past the threshold. Very strong: the same orders, but even the top belief cannot cover the high cost, so entry returns to its floor. The bounds hold for every order plan, so each of the three has one outcome.",
 r"At the weak strength, even the whole spread is below the order cost, so the informed trader does not trade and entry stays at its floor. At the strong strength, even the lowest gain exceeds the order cost, so the informed trader buys with good synergy and sells with poor synergy, and only a purchase lifts the belief past the threshold. At the very strong strength, the orders stay the same, but rival profit at the top belief does not cover the high cost, so entry returns to its floor. The bounds hold for every order plan, so each of the three strengths has one outcome."),
(r"So the rise must come from a change in what reaches the rival.", r"So the rise must come from a change in the rival's information."),
