(r"Privately chosen, prior one half. The recruiting equilibrium exists exactly when $\Delta_T>2k$ and $\tau\le M_{\hat\lambda}$. In it, research rises with the spread up to the cap. Total and good-synergy entry rise, and poor-synergy entry falls, because research replaces liquidity orders.",
 r"Assume ranked classes, $\pi=1/2$, $g_H>g_L$, $\tau>1/2$ and the default tie rules. Research is private, costs $a\lambda^2/2$ and has a cap $\bar\lambda<1$. For $\Delta_T>2k$, $\lambda_R$ solves $2a\lambda_R=\Delta_Tm_{\lambda_R}-k+(\rho\Delta_Tm_{\lambda_R}-k)_+$, and $\hat\lambda=\min\{\lambda_R,\bar\lambda\}$. The recruiting equilibrium exists exactly when $\Delta_T>2k$ and $\tau\le M_{\hat\lambda}$. In it, research rises with the spread up to the cap. Total and good-synergy entry rise, and poor-synergy entry falls, because research replaces liquidity orders."),
