# W1
(r"``Yes. In my example, a price near the top value earns more at all three strengths, and it stops recruitment. But that price sells only to a ready high-class rival, so it earns $\rho\pi h$, and it depends on how large that ready share is. Take one fifth in place of one quarter and keep everything else. The three conditions still hold, and the best reserve at each strength gives entry at the floor, then above it, then back at the floor. So the seller's choice limits this channel without removing it.''",
 r"``Yes, in my example a reserve near the top value earns more at all three strengths and stops recruitment. That reserve sells only to a ready rival with good synergy, so it earns $\rho\pi h$, and the result depends on the ready share. I change that share from one quarter to one fifth and keep the rest the same. The three conditions still hold, and the best reserve at each strength gives entry at its floor, then above its floor, then back at its floor. The seller's choice limits this channel without removing it.''"),
(r"No, and I do not claim that. The result holds", r"No. The result holds"),
